{"tag":"N9PG","body":"<div class=\"pq-q ue-math\"><p>Consider a decision maker who systematically calculates that <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"2+3=6.\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span> Construct a money-pump argument against him, and discuss the argument.</p></div><div class=\"pq-ans pq-ans--whole\" data-answer><p class=\"pq-ans-k\">Answer</p><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>A money pump exists. For instance, holding <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"2\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span> units he values <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"3\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span> more as bringing his holding to <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"6,\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">6</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span> so he pays nearly <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"4\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span></span></span></span></span></span> for them; holding <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"5\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span></span></span> he calculates correctly and sells the <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"3\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span> units back for just over <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"3.\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span> He ends where he started, poorer, and repeating the cycle extracts any amount.</p></div></div>"}